   "id": 372138,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>WorldCorp collects thousands of datasets every week. A large part of the managers’ jobs is monitoring this data, and they cannot monitor it efficiently if a workbook has mistakes. See this figure for a current dataset with some #VALUE! errors. What does this #VALUE! error code mean? What would you recommend doing in the formula audit process? What are the tools you would use, and how would you do it? Explain.</p>\n\n<table>\n<thead>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Operational Budget for the Fairfax, VA Manufacturing Plant</th>\n    <th></th>\n    <th></th>\n    <th></th>\n  </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n    <td></td>\n    <td></td>\n    <td></td>\n    <td></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><b>Component</b></td>\n    <td><b>Projected Cost</b></td>\n    <td><b>Actual Cost</b></td>\n    <td><b>Difference</b></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Direct Materials</td>\n    <td>$52,536,474.63</td>\n    <td>$56,436,363.00</td>\n    <td>$3,899,888.37</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Direct Labor</td>\n    <td>$64,236,234.33</td>\n    <td>$67,436,356.00</td>\n    <td>$3,200,121.37</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Manufacturing Overhead</td>\n    <td>$53,386,433.99</td>\n    <td>$52,453,476.00</td>\n    <td>#VALUE!</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Maintenance</td>\n    <td>$535,252.00</td>\n    <td>$446,736.00</td>\n    <td>$(88,516.00)</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Utility Services</td>\n    <td>$4,526,236.00</td>\n    <td>$5,736,363.00</td>\n    <td>$1,210,127.00</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Administrative Costs</td>\n    <td>$4,256,236.00</td>\n    <td>$4,156,477.00</td>\n    <td>$(100,296.00)</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Sales Costs</td>\n    <td>$7,755,674.64</td>\n    <td>$7,537,363.00</td>\n    <td>$(218,311.64)</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Depreciation</td>\n    <td>$85,670.00</td>\n    <td>$86,845.00</td>\n    <td>$1,175.00</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td></td>\n    <td> <br>$187,318,748.59 </td>\n    <td> <br>$137,853,616.00 </td>\n    <td> <br>#VALUE! </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
